      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_omni_directional_travel",
        "char_wu_yong",
        "house_clear_jade_dripping_wind_tiny_bamboo_building"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Silent hit, air lump growth, fixed range, time limit, and reverse flow reflection.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "move-mechanics",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Shadow Sect’s immortals do not know when the killer move struck them; without the sub-par Omni-directional Travel result they would have thought Wu Yong was bluffing. Fang Yuan has the others research air lock inside his immortal aperture while he flees on the upper extreme heavenly eagle. Light wind grows into an air lump on him, and two blue wind lumps entangle the eagle’s wings; Fang Yuan guesses the air lump is probably air lock and that it can absorb scattered winds to increase its power. The researchers call it a rank eight killer move. Wu Yong says that once the move is set up it cannot be shifted, that its range can cover the surrounding hundred thousand li, and that as of then it can still last for eight minutes. When reverse flow protection seal reflects the effect on Fang Yuan back to Wu Yong, the upper extreme heavenly eagle remains plagued by it, while Wu Yong inside Clear Jade Dripping Wind Tiny Bamboo Building is not affected.",
      "chapters": [
        1387
      ],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "move-mechanics",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_shadow_sect",
        "sys_killer_moves",
        "move_reverse_flow_protection_seal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Air lock has not timed out when Fang Yuan blocks the Immortal Gu House.",
      "chapters": [],
